% Regression tests for the sequential (non-random) fuzzing state machine
% FlagValue-backed fields (FlagsField) should be fuzzable like any other field

# Previously, return_relevant_fields() hard-skipped ANY field whose
# default_fields value was a concrete FlagValue/RSNCipherSuite/
# PMKIDListPacket instance, printing "Skipping: ... due to: FlagValue".
# That check was too broad: most FlagsFields (TCP.flags, IP.flags,
# Dot11.FCfield) were never actually concrete FlagValues to begin with -
# fuzz() already gives them a proper RandNum. The fields that really did
# stay concrete were ones wrapped in a ConditionalField whose condition
# wasn't satisfied when fuzz() ran (Dot11.FCfield2, gated on
# (type, subtype) == (3, 1)) - the same "this field doesn't apply right
# now" situation any other ConditionalField can be in, nothing specific to
# FlagValue.
#
# Fixed by replacing the hardcoded class-name skip lists (both the
# top-level one and the nested list-of-sub-packet one) with a single
# isinstance(field, VolatileValue) check: skip whatever is still concrete/
# unfuzzed, fuzz whatever genuinely is a VolatileValue, regardless of
# which concrete type it happens to be. This also newly makes
# ConditionalField-gated FlagsFields fuzzable whenever their condition IS
# satisfied - previously they were unconditionally skipped no matter what.

############
############
+ FlagValue-backed fields are fuzzable when their condition holds

= Same pattern for Dot11.FCfield2 (gated on (type, subtype) == (3, 1))
~ fuzzing dot11

not_gated = fuzz(Dot11())
assert not any('FCfield2' in f for f in not_gated.return_relevant_fields(not_gated))

gated = fuzz(Dot11(type=3, subtype=1))
assert any('FCfield2' in f for f in gated.return_relevant_fields(gated))
assert isinstance(gated.default_fields['FCfield2'], RandNum)


= Unconditional FlagsFields (TCP.flags, IP.flags) are unaffected
~ fuzzing dot11 inet

tcp = fuzz(TCP())
assert any(f.endswith(':flags') for f in tcp.return_relevant_fields(tcp))

ip = fuzz(IP(dst="192.168.1.1"))
assert any(f.endswith(':flags') for f in ip.return_relevant_fields(ip))


= RSNCipherSuite (a concrete PacketField value) is still correctly excluded
~ fuzzing dot11

rsn = fuzz(Dot11EltRSN())
fields = rsn.return_relevant_fields(rsn)
assert not any('group_cipher_suite' in f for f in fields)
